00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:53,620
Did something happen?

563
00:27:56,020 --> 00:27:57,820
I saw something I didn't want to see.

564
00:27:59,520 --> 00:28:01,460
What? What do you mean?

565
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:04,860
You know what?

566
00:28:05,560 --> 00:28:11,340
You have to be responsible for what you do.

567
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:15,400
What are you talking about?

568
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:17,280
I don't know what you're talking about.

569
00:28:19,520 --> 00:28:20,940
Don't be so stubborn.

570
00:28:23,220 --> 00:28:23,980
Do it.

571
00:28:24,520 --> 00:28:25,180
No.

572
00:28:28,480 --> 00:28:29,560
Hurry up and do it.

573
00:28:30,600 --> 00:28:31,740
Ms. Sawaiya.

574
00:28:34,280 --> 00:28:34,800
How was it?

575
00:28:35,680 --> 00:28:36,960
Did you get to talk to your mom?

576
00:28:39,120 --> 00:28:40,440
That's how it is.

577
00:28:40,440 --> 00:28:44,280
I don't think her way of thinking is going to change.

578
00:28:50,100 --> 00:28:53,180
I think you should go to college.

579
00:28:56,990 --> 00:29:00,000
I think what your mom says makes sense.

580
00:29:02,020 --> 00:29:03,580
But you only have one life.

581
00:29:04,170 --> 00:29:09,300
If you have any regrets, I don't think you should give up so easily.

582
00:29:13,500 --> 00:29:14,800
You have to live a life that you're satisfied with.

583
00:29:17,840 --> 00:29:20,640
Even so, it's a realistic problem.

584
00:29:22,680 --> 00:29:23,900
Like money?

585
00:29:25,460 --> 00:29:27,220
I see.

586
00:29:29,760 --> 00:29:30,660
There is a scholarship system.

587
00:29:31,760 --> 00:29:34,840
If you really want to go to college, I think you can do it.

588
00:29:35,940 --> 00:29:37,620
I'll look into it.

589
00:29:38,780 --> 00:29:39,700
It's not that much.

590
00:29:42,120 --> 00:29:44,220
It's not that much to go to college.

591
00:29:45,280 --> 00:29:47,340
You don't have to spend time for me.

592
00:29:48,200 --> 00:29:49,220
You don't have to push yourself.

593
00:29:49,640 --> 00:29:51,580
But Ms. Sawaiya...

594
00:29:51,580 --> 00:29:52,900
I don't want to bother you.

595
00:29:53,820 --> 00:29:55,140
I'll take care of myself.

596
00:29:57,680 --> 00:29:58,440
It's not a bother.

597
00:30:00,480 --> 00:30:01,800
It's not a bother.

598
00:30:23,140 --> 00:30:25,740
Hey, how are you?

599
00:30:25,740 --> 00:30:26,460
Hi.

600
00:30:27,100 --> 00:30:28,300
I have a favor to ask of you.

601
00:30:29,640 --> 00:30:30,600
Yes?

602
00:30:31,440 --> 00:30:33,200
Good morning.

603
00:30:33,860 --> 00:30:35,080
Good morning.

604
00:30:37,040 --> 00:30:38,340
What's going on?

605
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:42,480
Ms. Iro!

606
00:30:42,740 --> 00:30:45,080
The police just called!

607
00:30:45,820 --> 00:30:46,820
The police?

608
00:30:54,100 --> 00:30:56,780
Is it okay to go inside?

609
00:30:57,780 --> 00:31:00,540
Or should I park in a coin park nearby?

610
00:31:02,040 --> 00:31:04,740
By the way, what's the parking fee in this case?

611
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:06,060
It's free.

612
00:31:09,360 --> 00:31:10,220
I'm sorry.

613
00:31:11,380 --> 00:31:13,720
I'm sorry, sir.

614
00:31:14,300 --> 00:31:17,300
I'm sorry for bothering you.

615
00:31:17,520 --> 00:31:19,960
I thought you were going to call me.

616
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:21,000
I thought you were going to call me.

617
00:31:21,020 --> 00:31:22,760
But you insisted on contacting the teacher.

618
00:31:23,860 --> 00:31:26,000
I told you many times.

619
00:31:26,880 --> 00:31:29,580
We know who his father is.

620
00:31:30,780 --> 00:31:31,900
You know him, right?

621
00:31:32,360 --> 00:31:32,940
Yes.

622
00:31:33,780 --> 00:31:35,420
If your father finds out, he'll kill you.

623
00:31:37,560 --> 00:31:39,180
What about Kouken?

624
00:31:41,380 --> 00:31:45,300
The local gangsters had a fight with the gangsters in other areas.

625
00:31:45,300 --> 00:31:47,060
I'm sorry.

626
00:31:47,060 --> 00:31:48,740
He's a car driver.

627
00:31:49,180 --> 00:31:50,020
He's not involved in the fight.

628
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:51,640
He's not allowed to drive.

629
00:31:52,320 --> 00:31:54,000
I'm sorry.

630
00:31:54,580 --> 00:31:55,120
I'm really sorry.

631
00:31:55,120 --> 00:31:57,860
I stopped him for a night because I couldn't find him.

632
00:31:58,500 --> 00:32:00,420
Other gangsters found him.

633
00:32:02,940 --> 00:32:05,820
I'm sorry.

634
00:32:08,040 --> 00:32:08,760
I'm really sorry.

635
00:32:09,260 --> 00:32:09,700
I'm really sorry.

636
00:32:10,120 --> 00:32:13,020
I'm really sorry.

637
00:32:14,020 --> 00:32:14,820
I'm sorry.

638
00:32:14,820 --> 00:32:16,520
If you don't talk to him, you're banned from the school.

639
00:32:17,380 --> 00:32:18,300
OK.

640
00:32:18,600 --> 00:32:19,840
Let's talk about other things.

641
00:32:21,400 --> 00:32:22,760
Kouken, let's talk.

642
00:32:23,500 --> 00:32:24,420
What?

643
00:32:24,420 --> 00:32:24,480
I'm sorry.

644
00:32:24,540 --> 00:32:26,040
I'll take him home, ok?

645
00:32:26,740 --> 00:32:27,660
OK.

646
00:32:29,340 --> 00:32:31,400
I'll talk to your father.

647
00:32:34,740 --> 00:32:36,700
Do you talk to your father often?

648
00:32:37,720 --> 00:32:38,640
Almost.

649
00:32:39,980 --> 00:32:40,900
I see.

650
00:32:41,780 --> 00:32:42,220
Why?

651
00:32:42,220 --> 00:32:44,140
I don't know.

652
00:32:44,140 --> 00:32:45,800
My father is busy and I don't talk to him.

653
00:32:50,020 --> 00:32:51,540
Do you know why he quit Yakuza?

654
00:32:54,420 --> 00:32:55,180
Do you know?

655
00:32:56,100 --> 00:32:57,520
Yakuza is bad these days.

656
00:32:58,080 --> 00:32:58,990
It's not because he doesn't like it.

657
00:32:59,500 --> 00:33:00,460
Did your father say that?

658
00:33:01,240 --> 00:33:02,220
I don't know.

659
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:05,480
He used to say it was good, but now it's not.

660
00:33:08,320 --> 00:33:09,080
I see.

661
00:33:09,080 --> 00:33:10,820
Do you have a reason?

662
00:33:12,300 --> 00:33:14,380
Do you know why I don't know?

663
00:33:15,440 --> 00:33:17,680
It's like this for a man and a woman.

664
00:33:20,380 --> 00:33:20,880
What?

665
00:33:22,660 --> 00:33:27,400
Did you play with your father often?

666
00:33:29,080 --> 00:33:30,080
Yes.

667
00:33:31,280 --> 00:33:32,640
I see.

668
00:33:34,700 --> 00:33:36,040
What do you mean?

669
00:33:42,960 --> 00:33:49,900
My father wanted me to go to college.

670
00:33:52,040 --> 00:33:52,940
You don't want to say that.

671
00:33:56,320 --> 00:33:58,440
It doesn't matter if you go to college.

672
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:01,100
You're right.

673
00:34:02,080 --> 00:34:03,060
You're right.

674
00:34:05,080 --> 00:34:07,480
There are people who think that going to college is no good.

675
00:34:08,980 --> 00:34:09,060
I'm sorry.

676
00:34:09,060 --> 00:34:12,340
I understand that.

677
00:34:12,340 --> 00:34:16,380
But I don't want you to go to college.

678
00:34:19,660 --> 00:34:21,580
What do you mean?

679
00:34:22,960 --> 00:34:26,340
I want you to be happy.

680
00:34:27,340 --> 00:34:34,720
I want you to be happy by going to college.

681
00:34:36,060 --> 00:34:41,180
I want you to go to college because I feel the possibility.

682
00:34:41,180 --> 00:34:42,600
I'm sure of it.

683
00:34:43,640 --> 00:34:47,740
If you want to go to college, I'll go with you.

684
00:34:47,740 --> 00:34:48,940
Do you want to do your best?

685
00:34:49,700 --> 00:34:50,840
I can't do that.

686
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:55,600
I'm a beginner now.

687
00:34:56,240 --> 00:34:58,360
I have to level up to go to college.

688
00:34:59,280 --> 00:35:00,340
Let's do our best.

689
00:35:01,320 --> 00:35:02,560
What are you doing?

690
00:35:02,560 --> 00:35:03,960
Why don't you leave me alone?

691
00:35:05,180 --> 00:35:08,180
I don't want to get involved with you.

692
00:35:08,180 --> 00:35:10,300
I told my father that I wanted to quit yakuza.

693
00:35:13,760 --> 00:35:14,700
It's a promise.

694
00:35:16,940 --> 00:35:17,820
What?

695
00:35:19,700 --> 00:35:20,980
What do you mean?

696
00:35:21,120 --> 00:35:23,580
I don't want you to walk the same path as me.

697
00:35:25,220 --> 00:35:26,680
I don't want you to become a yakuza.

698
00:35:26,680 --> 00:35:27,260
I don't want you to do that.

699
00:35:28,200 --> 00:35:30,140
I can't be a yakuza without a message.

700
00:35:34,420 --> 00:35:38,620
Your father was crying.

701
00:35:42,660 --> 00:35:45,720
He was crying while making ramen with me and Mr. Ryo.

702
00:35:49,320 --> 00:35:51,280
He was so powerful.

703
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:53,280
You know, your father...

704
00:35:55,900 --> 00:35:57,900
You're the one who loves me the most,

705
00:35:58,320 --> 00:35:59,260
but you don't have to be like that.

706
00:36:00,840 --> 00:36:01,320
Right?

707
00:36:03,220 --> 00:36:04,180
Let's go to school.

708
00:36:05,180 --> 00:36:05,880
I'll bring you some food.

709
00:36:07,980 --> 00:36:09,940
But don't tell everyone that I brought you food.

710
00:36:11,120 --> 00:36:11,600
I will.

711
00:36:11,600 --> 00:36:13,520
Say hello to Mr. Ryo and Mr. Kyoto.

712
00:36:15,300 --> 00:36:16,260
Okay.

713
00:36:17,120 --> 00:36:18,920
And if you want to study, come to my house.

714
00:36:19,160 --> 00:36:19,740
Okay.

715
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:22,640
Hello.

716
00:36:23,500 --> 00:36:24,060
Ryo.

717
00:36:24,300 --> 00:36:25,400
You're late.

718
00:36:26,140 --> 00:36:26,940
You're late.

719
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:28,020
How long have you been sleeping?

720
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:29,000
I'm not sleeping.

721
00:36:30,180 --> 00:36:32,840
Mr. Okido, I have a suggestion for today.

722
00:36:34,120 --> 00:36:34,960
What is it?

723
00:36:35,620 --> 00:36:37,120
Would you like to lend me the notes for this morning's class?

724
00:36:41,660 --> 00:36:42,660
Sugiyama.

725
00:36:44,720 --> 00:36:45,220
I'll lend it to you.

726
00:36:47,900 --> 00:36:48,980
Thank you.

727
00:36:49,400 --> 00:36:50,000
Are you going to quit?

728
00:36:50,000 --> 00:36:50,860
Yeah.

729
00:36:54,480 --> 00:36:54,960
Let's go.

730
00:36:56,920 --> 00:36:57,620
Okay.

731
00:36:59,480 --> 00:37:00,960
You're pretty late.

732
00:37:24,740 --> 00:37:26,260
Excuse me.

733
00:37:27,500 --> 00:37:28,360
I'm sorry.

734
00:37:28,860 --> 00:37:29,540
I brought Kougen here.

735
00:37:30,960 --> 00:37:32,140
Oh, I heard.

736
00:37:34,080 --> 00:37:36,000
Kougen wants to get out of here.

737
00:37:40,240 --> 00:37:41,000
Mr. Ryo.

738
00:37:47,600 --> 00:37:48,940
He did it.

739
00:37:48,960 --> 00:37:49,600
He's a pro.

740
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:49,840
He's a pro.

741
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:49,980
He's a pro.

742
00:37:50,980 --> 00:37:52,560
Aika, you're drinking too much.

743
00:37:54,800 --> 00:37:55,340
Hit him.

744
00:38:38,480 --> 00:38:39,100
Right.

745
00:38:39,240 --> 00:38:39,920
I'm sorry, it's hot.

746
00:38:52,180 --> 00:38:56,200
You look like you're having a good time.

747
00:38:59,440 --> 00:39:00,980
Dad...

748
00:39:02,900 --> 00:39:05,640
Do I look like this when I wash my feet?

749
00:39:07,260 --> 00:39:08,260
You idiot.

750
00:39:09,500 --> 00:39:10,520
That's a hundred times better.

751
00:39:22,320 --> 00:39:27,240
Here you go.

752
00:39:35,540 --> 00:39:37,140
Thanks for the food.

753
00:39:51,460 --> 00:39:54,520
I've had a lot of trouble since April.

754
00:39:56,640 --> 00:39:58,520
You took me here last time.

755
00:40:00,600 --> 00:40:02,200
I see.

756
00:40:03,640 --> 00:40:04,780
It ended in the evening.

757
00:40:08,800 --> 00:40:11,540
You really care about me, don't you?

758
00:40:13,920 --> 00:40:15,480
I see.

759
00:40:17,440 --> 00:40:18,240
I'm glad.

760
00:40:24,240 --> 00:40:27,040
I'm sorry.

761
00:40:31,360 --> 00:40:32,240
It hurts, but...

762
00:40:32,240 --> 00:40:35,320
It hurts, but...

763
00:40:35,520 --> 00:40:36,840
It's so good.

764
00:40:52,100 --> 00:40:53,940
I'm sorry.

765
00:40:55,920 --> 00:40:56,400
For all the trouble.

766
00:41:06,400 --> 00:41:07,800
Dad.

767
00:41:24,380 --> 00:41:27,100
Thank you.

768
00:41:49,980 --> 00:41:54,900
I can't get over my own weakness

769
00:41:55,980 --> 00:41:58,320
But, you know,

770
00:41:58,660 --> 00:42:03,520
Everyone is full of worries

771
00:42:03,520 --> 00:42:09,400
I'm still alive today while searching

772
00:42:09,400 --> 00:42:16,960
I'll send you a song

773
00:42:16,960 --> 00:42:24,180
Stopping my tears for just one moment

774
00:42:25,670 --> 00:42:29,980
I will sing this song for you, my friend

775
00:42:29,980 --> 00:42:33,080
Sing this song with love

776
00:42:33,690 --> 00:42:39,060
Sing this song with sympathy and empathy

777
00:42:39,060 --> 00:42:42,820
Just by not noticing

778
00:42:42,820 --> 00:42:46,440
Love is overflowing

779
00:42:46,580 --> 00:42:50,480
In everything around you


